# awsbox AI workflow

Same shape as Colony / Funds Manager. Board: [Project #8](https://github.com/users/kgz/projects/8/views/1).

## Ticket first

```bash
export AWSBOX_AGENT=cursor-main   # Project #8 field Agent — not a GitHub label
./bin/board-status.sh in-progress <issue-num>
# or: ./bin/board-status.sh in-progress <n> --agent=cursor-main
```

Claim ownership via the board’s **Agent** text field (set on `in-progress`, cleared on `done`/`backlog`/`ready`). No per-agent labels.

Web UI / console tickets start in **designing** (see Open Design below), then move to **in-progress** for implementation.

Closing: `./bin/board-status.sh done <n>`. Keep `bin/board-tracker.tsv` in sync, then `./bin/board-audit.sh --apply`.

Lifecycle: **Backlog** → **Ready** → **Designing** → **In progress** → **In review** → **Done**.

## Versioning (milestones + release label)

- **Milestone** = service catalogue (`v1 — Networking`, …). Keep these names.
- **Label** = product release (`v0.0.1`, …) from `docs/CURRENT_RELEASE`. Catalogue “v1” work at the start of product versioning = label **`v0.0.1`**.
- Creating issues / Debt: assign milestone **and** add label `$(cat docs/CURRENT_RELEASE)`.
- **In progress / in review** → label `$(cat docs/CURRENT_RELEASE)` only (remove other `v0.0.x`). `v0.0.2`/`v0.0.3` are for backlog planning until the card is active.
- Cut a release (git tag + GitHub Release + new label + bump CURRENT_RELEASE): `./bin/release-tag.sh vX.Y.Z`. Details: `docs/versioning.md`.

## Branch

```bash
git checkout main && git pull origin main
git checkout -b feature/<issue>-<short-slug>
```

## Product north star

`docs/vision.md` — long-term feel (not a ticket).
OpenSpec changes are for **one delivery**; don’t park the whole product vision there.

## OpenSpec

- On `main`: `/opsx-propose` → `openspec/changes/<change-name>/`
- Delivery branch: `/opsx-apply` against `tasks.md`
- Grow `openspec/specs/` as shipped behaviour (archive changes separately)

## Open Design (required before web UI)

Any ticket that adds or changes **console / web UI** (`console/`, new service pages, chrome) must go through Open Design **before** React implementation:

1. `./bin/board-status.sh designing <n>` (also set by `./bin/od-design-run.sh --issue <n>`)
2. Theme: `design/awsbox/` (grey rose). Do not invent a new palette or copy AWS orange / sky blue / smile.
3. Mocks: `./bin/od-design-run.sh --issue <n> "…"`. Prefer skill **web-clone** when the screen exists in real AWS. Read-only AWS console screenshots are allowed; never create/update/delete real resources without explicit approval.
4. **Dead controls:** a button/link that is not wired yet must be `disabled` with `title="To implement"` (and a Debt ticket if it belongs in v1). If we will never ship it, omit it from the mock — do not leave an enabled control that does nothing or only toasts.
5. Land HTML under `design/awsbox-console/` (or the ticket’s design folder).
6. Only then `./bin/board-status.sh in-progress <n>` and implement against the mocks.

Never raw `curl` for OD runs — always `./bin/od-design-run.sh`.

## Commits / PRs

- No `Co-authored-by` / Cursor attribution
- PR body: `Closes #<n>`

## Gap check before `done` (required)

User relies on the agent to not lose half-baked follow-ups (especially UI stubs).

**Before** `./bin/board-status.sh done <n>` / merge:

```bash
./bin/gap-check.sh <n>
```

1. Walk the checklist in `docs/gap-check.md`
2. For every Partial / disabled Create / sidecar / “use CLI smoke” / authz hole / AWS console UI left out of v1 **without** an open Debt ticket → create `Debt: … (from #<n>)`, `backlog`, label `$(cat docs/CURRENT_RELEASE)`, tracker row, link from README or service doc. Console debt designs use Open Design `web-clone` (`./bin/od-design-run.sh`)
3. Mention new Debt issues in the PR body

Do **not** mark the parent done until gaps are ticketed (or explicitly N/A in the PR).
